en:
I know something about London;
I have been to Paris and Rome only briefly;
I have never visited Constantinople at all.

Thus the day flows away
through the sink
when I wash my hands;

Some of the authors are
introspective as well as critical;
some try to find a way out
of their academic predicament;
some sigh with regret
that Redology is faced with a crisis;

faces that dared not smile一
to express joy;
faces that dared not
refrain from a forced smile
when there was no joy at all
to justify a smile;

I do not fear natural death
for nobody can avoid it,
hence no use fearing.

Each room, I remember,
had an electric lamp hanging from the ceiling.
The drawing room had a 50-watt bulb;
the bedrooms each a lower-wattage one;
the kitchens each an even-lower-wattage one.

This torrent is always surging ahead;
it has never stopped for a single moment
and will never stop.

I'll be in a real fix
if they should rob me of,
say, my bedding or clothes.

